* Removing one prime factor ` P ` of a squarefree ` W ` at most halves the number of divisors up to ` y ` (AGP (4.1) for one prime): the divisors of ` W ` lie in the divisors of ` W / P ` together with their ` P ` -multiples (~ coprmdvds , ~ dvdscmulr , ~ bmhashim ).

